{"byteLength":399,"contentHash":{"algorithm":"sha256","value":"38e10aa8f36e84e566ff439400579ea40291997da1b6393f2ead872eae99340e"},"kind":"skillDocument","name":"references/stdlib/Lazy.md","producer":{"build":{"commit":"5de2594ad523fba4f38fa63f7a1b306e8a23eb0c","dirty":false,"provenance":{"commit":"git","dirty":"environment"},"target":"aarch64-apple-darwin"},"name":"benitoite","version":"0.0.13"},"schemaVersion":1,"text":"# Benitoite.Lazy\n\nStatus: standard, in the prelude. It can be used without `import`.\n\nRefer to its declarations as `Lazy.<name>`, for example `Lazy.force`.\n\nExplicitly delayed values, made with `lazy ... end lazy`. The type `Lazy` is built in.\n\n```benitoite\npublic function force[T](value: Lazy[T]) -> T\n```\n\nEvaluates the delayed body on the first call and returns the remembered value afterwards.\n"}
